  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One descriptor per resource",
      "items": [
        "A resource file declares an assignment descriptor and registers newAssignmentResource(descriptor) in init()",
        "The descriptor names the identity attributes, the allowed grant types and the scope adapter (NewAdapter)",
        "The factory derives the schema, the internal ID and import format, and Create, Read, Update, Delete"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Reconcile",
      "items": [
        "Update reconciles to the configured grant types; Delete reconciles to the empty set",
        "Create first fails if the assignee already holds a direct grant at the scope (import it instead), then writes the difference",
        "Read stores the assignee's current direct grants, so changes made outside Terraform show up as drift",
        "Grants that other assignees hold at the scope are never revoked; a failed read never leads to a write"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Extending the module",
      "items": [
        "Scope adapters are the only assignment code that calls *api.Client",
        "New grant type: add it to the descriptor's grant types",
        "New kind of scope: add a scope adapter (assignment_adapter_<scope>.go) and the *api.Client methods it calls",
        "New assignee at an existing scope: add a resource file with a new descriptor"
      ]
    }
  ]
